WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.910
URS HOLZLE: Last year, we
committed to continuously drive

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:06.430
down costs for our customers
in alignment with Moore's law.

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:09.150
And since then, we announced
three major price reductions.

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.520
And we continue to
lead the industry

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.910
in combining strong performance
with low cost as well

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:17.550
as flexible, commitment-free
pricing options.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.640
We believe Google Cloud Platform
delivers better performance

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.820
at lower cost than
other cloud providers.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:26.370
You may wonder how
we're able to do this.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:28.350
First, we're creating
infrastructure

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.810
that's tailored to your
workload, not the other way

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:31.470
around.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:34.080
Earlier this year, we
introduced nearline storage

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.740
to dramatically reduce
storage costs by up to 70%

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:40.440
for many classes of
content and data.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.740
And more recently, we
announced preemptible VMs,

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.140
a new class of machine
tailored specifically

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:49.560
for stateless applications,
such as Hadoop processing

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:51.540
and short-duration
batch workloads.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:54.840
Preemptible VMs can lower
your costs by as much as 70%

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.580
compared to standard VMs.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:59.550
And they're perfect for adding
firepower to data processing

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:00.720
applications.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.600
Secondly, we provide you with
the most appropriate billing

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:06.720
plan so you can save
on costs automatically.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:08.730
You shouldn't have to
spend hours or days

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:11.880
calculating rate plans in
different classes of machines.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.020
We believe that the cloud
should do that for you.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:17.040
And for that reason,
we pioneered a number

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.340
of innovations in pricing,
including per-minute billing

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:22.170
and sustained use discounts.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:25.230
Options such as these
significantly lower your cost

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:27.150
and are provided to
you automatically.

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:29.550
Third, we don't force
you to prepay to get

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:31.470
the discounts you deserve.

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:34.290
Signing long-term contracts
reduces your flexibility

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:36.210
in a rapidly
changing environment.

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:39.060
As your business grows, the
types of compute resources

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:40.600
you need change as well.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.500
For example, you may start
off on a standard VM.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:45.810
But as you grow, a
new class of machine

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:47.670
may result in dramatic savings.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:50.480
Reserved instance pricing
or other prepay schemes

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.780
lock you not only
into the price,

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:55.740
but also into a machine
class and a location.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.630
This works only
if you don't grow

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:59.610
or if you have a very
good crystal ball.

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:03.000
So we give you the flexibility
to change regions or classes

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.010
of machines to meet
your changing business

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:06.720
needs with no penalty.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:09.509
And finally, we're establishing
firm price performance

00:02:09.509 --> 00:02:11.610
benchmarks based on Moore's Law.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.830
So as infrastructure
becomes more efficient

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:16.560
and the price of the underlying
hardware continues to decline,

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.290
we are committed to pass
those savings on to you.

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:21.660
So taken together,
we want to make sure

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:23.820
that our cloud platform
provides the lowest

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:26.730
total cost of ownership and
the highest performance.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:31.580
[MUSIC PLAYING]

